WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.903 --> 00:00:19.221
Sign in as the business owner.

2
00:00:19.321 --> 00:00:25.919
Open People, then Customers. Every customer in your book is listed here with phone, email and balance.

3
00:00:27.219 --> 00:00:32.804
The tabs above the table split customers by status: all, active, inactive and archived.

4
00:00:32.905 --> 00:00:38.602
Search by name, phone, email or ID. Type part of a name and the list narrows as you type.

5
00:00:40.203 --> 00:00:44.856
Tick "Customers who owe" to see only customers with an unpaid balance.

6
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.783
To add someone new, click New customer.

7
00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:57.469
Only a name and one way to reach them are required. Start with the first and last name.

8
00:00:57.569 --> 00:01:02.993
Add a phone number and an email. The customer card on the right updates as you type.

9
00:01:03.094 --> 00:01:09.175
Optional details such as address, customer group and credit limit can be filled in now or later.

10
00:01:09.275 --> 00:01:11.919
Click Create customer to save.

11
00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:19.075
The new customer is at the top of the list. Click the name to open their profile.

12
00:01:19.175 --> 00:01:24.816
The profile gathers contact details, purchases, payments, credit and notes in one place.

13
00:01:24.916 --> 00:01:33.499
For a customer who has bought before, the profile shows the balance and everything they spent.

14
00:01:33.599 --> 00:01:39.193
Balance is what the customer still owes you. Collect a payment from here when they pay.

15
00:01:39.294 --> 00:01:45.485
The Purchase history tab lists every sale to this customer, so you can answer "what did they buy?"

16
00:01:46.786 --> 00:01:53.363
That is the customer book. Add people at the counter or here, and their history builds up with each sale.
